BY DESIGN, NOT BY MERIT. This directory is the CONTROL arm of test-defcon2-holdfire-ambush.
Its rules.yaml differs from the treatment's by exactly one quantity --
DefconEscalation.ModeDefault, Escalation -> Skirmish -- and DefconEscalationState's
constructor answers that with `Level = NoLevel` (0), so AutoTarget.INotifyDamage.Damaged no
longer returns at its first line.

The chain then runs end to end: the ordered shot damages the bait, the handler proceeds, the
bait is in Ambush so it sets its own latch AND calls TriggerNearbyAmbushAllies (read site 6),
each ally inside the 10-cell AmbushCoordinationRadius has ambushTriggered written for it, and
on its next idle tick AmbushTickIdle's `if (isSpotted || ambushTriggered)` is satisfied by the
SECOND term alone. The allies fire and the shared body's ally-ammunition assertion fails.
FAIL is the only outcome this arm can honestly produce.

READ `seen=` ON THE ALLIES BEFORE READING ANYTHING ELSE. The whole value of this arm rests on
the allies being UNDETECTABLE to USA, which is what makes `isSpotted` false and leaves the
proxy as the only thing that can have sprung them. Every census line carries `seen=false` per
ally. If any reads `seen=true`, the geometry has drifted, the allies could have sprung
themselves through detection, and this run is evidence about detection rather than about read
site 6 -- discard it and fix the vision arithmetic (rules.yaml raises the t90s'
Detectable.Vision to 7 against a strength-6 reading at fourteen cells; ^Vehicle's
DetectableAddativeModifier@Stationary adds one more).

A PASS HERE IS LOUDLY RED AND FALSIFIES THE TREATMENT, NOT THIS FILE. It would mean an ambush
lane did not light off when one of its members was shot, in an ordinary Skirmish -- so the
stances, the coordination radius or the trigger is wrong in BOTH directories and the
treatment's silence was measuring nothing. Report and stop.

THE ONE FAILURE THIS DECLARATION MUST NOT ABSORB, because it produces the declared outcome for
the wrong reason: a staging fault. Verdicts beginning `fail: SETUP` (an ally out of weapon
range or outside the coordination radius, no ammunition, the match opened at DEFCON 3 or 1),
`fail: ATTRIBUTION` (an ally visible to USA, or the bait invisible to it) and `fail: the
ORDERED shot never hit the bait` are faults in BOTH directories. That last one is the most
important to notice: it means the trigger was never delivered, so nothing was ever asked of
the proxy and the run says nothing about either arm.

A failure naming the BAIT rather than an ally is read site 2, not site 6. The shared body
checks the bait ONCE, at the END of the observation window, precisely so this arm always runs
long enough to reach the ally verdict first; a bait-only failure here means the allies held in
Skirmish, which is the PASS case above wearing a different hat and should be treated as one.

REMOVE THIS FILE only if the control legitimately starts passing, which would mean the map can
no longer separate the two hypotheses and needs new geometry rather than a new declaration. A
hang, a crash, or a run that never reaches a verdict still reds under it.
